{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Look, etc.</b> The prophet recounts the prayer of the maskilim in exile, for it is joined with what he fought against them <small>(above 10)</small>:" "<b>From the habitation of</b>, like dwelling, and similarly 'my husband will lodge with me' <small>(Genesis 30:21)</small>, and behold the meaning is doubled:" "<b> restrain yourself.</b> Now, like 'and Joseph could not restrain himself' <small>(Genesis 45:1)</small>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {0 "The antecedent of 'he' in 'he fought against them' is ambiguous in the Hebrew; left unresolved.", 1 "Rendered מזבול per the lemma; Ibn Ezra reads it as 'habitation/dwelling' from the root ז-ב-ל."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:51.779883267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}